{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Work targets the existing open-source repositories: spring-cloud-dataflow (s-c-d), spring-cloud-stream (s-c-s), and spring-cloud-stream-modules (s-c-s-m), using their existing build system (Maven/Gradle) and code conventions.",
    "For U1, deployment properties will be modeled as a generic Map<String,String> passed through the deployment pipeline; the reserved 'count' key will be interpreted by the deployer to launch N module instances that share the same environment variables.",
    "For U2, GitHub Pages publishing will use a gh-pages branch per repository with docs generated (Asciidoctor/Markdown) and pushed as part of PR/commit workflow via the existing CI hooks.",
    "For U3, the Kafka binder fix will be validated with integration tests using an embedded/Dockerized Kafka plus a manual verification run against an operational external broker.",
    "For U6, the RxJava processor module will be implemented as a standard Spring Cloud Stream processor (input/output channels) following the s-c-s-m module structure, with unit and integration tests.",
    "For U7, the banner will be implemented as a Spring Boot banner.txt resource in the shell server module, generated with a TAAG-style ASCII generator.",
    "All documentation (U4, U8) will be written in the repositories' existing documentation format and structure (Asciidoc reference docs for U4, Markdown README for U8).",
    "Java/JVM baseline follows the target framework versions of the s-c-d 1.x/2.x era being maintained; the Spring Framework 6.0 / Java 17 note applies only where relevant to newer modules."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All work is performed by a single developer (myself), and estimates represent development effort in work-hours, not elapsed calendar time.",
    "Estimates include design, coding, unit testing, and integration testing within each activity; a separate cross-cutting activity covers integration/regression testing and review rework across stories.",
    "Access to the GitHub repositories, write/branch permissions (including gh-pages), CI infrastructure, and an operational Kafka broker for testing is available.",
    "The Kafka binder issue (U3) is a single, moderately complex defect requiring diagnosis and a targeted fix, not a full binder rewrite.",
    "No external review by other team members is required beyond self-review; minor review/merge rework is included in the cross-cutting activity.",
    "Study/research activities (U5) include producing a short findings summary and a proof-of-concept pipeline, not a full production CI migration.",
    "Existing test infrastructure (JUnit, Spring integration test support, embedded Kafka) can be reused without major upgrades."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Deployment properties with count support",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement support for optional key-value deployment properties in s-c-d, including the 'count' property to deploy N instances of modules sharing the same environment variables. Includes parsing/API changes, deployer integration, unit tests, and integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Set up gh-pages branches for s-c-d and s-c-s-m",
      "activity_description": "Create and configure gh-pages branches for the spring-cloud-dataflow and spring-cloud-stream-modules repositories, wire documentation publishing so docs are pushed with PR commits, and verify rendering on GitHub Pages.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Fix Kafka binder in spring-cloud-stream",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce and diagnose the Kafka binder defect, implement the fix, add/extend unit and integration tests (embedded Kafka), and verify that messaging microservices successfully bind to an operational external Kafka broker.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - s-c-d architecture reference documentation",
      "activity_description": "Author reference documentation describing the spring-cloud-dataflow architecture, explicitly defining the deployment differences between 1.x and 2.x, in the existing Asciidoc documentation structure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Study Concourse CI for s-c-d",
      "activity_description": "Study Concourse CI concepts and documentation, evaluate applicability to s-c-d builds, and produce a short findings summary plus a proof-of-concept pipeline definition.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 - RxJava processor module with Spring Cloud Stream",
      "activity_description": "Implement a sample processor module applying RxJava with spring-cloud-stream (input/output bindings), including unit tests, integration tests against a binder, and minimal usage documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Shell server startup banner",
      "activity_description": "Create a new ASCII-art banner (using a TAAG-style generator) and embed it as a Spring Boot banner resource displayed when the s-c-d shell server boots up; verify startup output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8 - 'Running on Cloud Foundry' README section",
      "activity_description": "Write and publish the 'Running on Cloud Foundry' section in the s-c-d README as a public deployment guideline, including steps, configuration, and verification notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration, regression testing, and review rework",
      "activity_description": "Run full builds and regression suites across affected modules, perform integration testing of the increment as a whole, address merge conflicts and review/rework findings, and prepare the increment for release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 200
  }
}
```

